From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:40:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SNES on a GPU

With a GPU (vectors of PETSc of the GPU, memory of MFEM managed by
Umpire), mfem::PetscNonlinearSolver::Mult placed the memory of the
unknowns in the vector of PETSc and left it in a state unknown to the
memory manager of MFEM, and __mfem_snes_jacobian gave to GetGradient the
array of the host of PETSc, unknown to it: the program stopped. SNES now
computes on vectors of PETSc of the host, created and read through their
arrays, and the functions called by PETSc (residual, tangent operator
seen as a shell matrix, with its transposed product for the trust region
methods, shell preconditioner) copy the vectors given by MFEM from and
to vectors of mfem-mgis on the host. The linear solvers of PETSc (option
LinearSolver set to PETSc) are refused when hypre computes on a GPU: the
Newton steps computed with the tangent operator converted to the AIJ
format were wrong (the Krylov solvers of PETSc of the factory of linear
solvers are also wrong on a GPU, to be investigated).

SNESSolverTestP-gpu: all the cases of SNESSolverTest but the linear
solvers of PETSc give the solution and the iterations of the Newton
solver on a GPU.
